  "id": "hearth",
  "name": "Hearth",
  "note": "The first rung of the ladder of skeletal economies: a village that feeds, clothes, tools and houses itself. Seventeen goods, sixteen recipes (five of them extractions on a site, with a limit), four consumers, and numbers on all of them, so the balance sheet can be watched while they are changed. One loop: the byre eats grain, and its dung goes back on the fields. Made by tools/make_hearth.py, which is the baseline; this file is the experiment.",
